      "texts": [
        "Tissue leaves the block. Data can be copied.",
        "A finite tissue block becomes a smaller remaining block as sections are allocated to slides and extraction. One-way arrows carry physical material into those uses; stored slides can remain, while extraction changes the material and loses its original architecture. A separate digital dataset branches into two copies with no reverse arrow to the original block. No universal section thickness, test count or allocation is prescribed.",
