    {
      "path": "wiki/education/concepts/measurement/specimens/images/fixed-frozen-viable-preserved-properties-b10-v1-light.svg",
      "sourceSHA256": "4268a579a2d7a030e10a2b3a5f9d933301f30a647be8f794db083b05ee8a10c7",
      "texts": [
        "Same tissue, different preserved options",
        "Three aligned preparation scenes show a fixed wax block and thin section, a snap-frozen tissue piece with a molecular-analysis symbol, and a viable cell aliquot beside a recovery and identity check. Fixed material preserves architecture but cannot recover original living cells; frozen material preserves analytes without guaranteeing viability; viable material needs workflow-specific recovery and function checks. There is no universal best preparation.",
