      "texts": [
        "Where did this result come from?",
        "A fictional oriented specimen has keyed superior and lateral outer surfaces, a selected central region A and surface region B, and visible unselected space. Each selected region connects to its own labeled tissue block. A fictional test result is attached only to block A, while block B and unselected tissue remain outside that result. The local ink key is invented and no margin-clearance claim is made.",
        "Where did this result",
        "come from?",
        "Fictional oriented specimen map",
        "A",
        "B",
        "Blue = superior; rose = lateral",
        "Unselected tissue stays visible.",
        "Keep the selected block identity",
        "A",
        "B",
        "Result from A → region A only",
        "Not B or every region.",
        "No clearance claim.",
        "Local key and map are invented."
      ],
